! shut / no shut an interface
bounce interface gi0/0


!
service log-hidden

! this doesn't show error counters on the stack ports
! TODO - find the show platform command that does
sh switch stack-ports detail


! if ZTP is allowed to run, the switch will configure itself for IPv6.
! if ZTP is interrupted as soon as boot up is complete, the switch will not have any IPv6 configuration.
! this has caused problems when trying to license 9300s.  the dns query would return both A and AAAA records.
!   the switch would then only use the AAAA record and would only try to connect to the licensing server via IPv6.
!   if your network isn't configured to use IPv6, licensing would fail.
! to remove IPv6:
!
int vlan 1
 no ipv6 enable
 no ipv6 dhcp client request vendor
 no ipv6 address dhcp
 no ipv6 address autoconfig
!
int gi0/0
 no ipv6 enable
 no ipv6 dhcp client request vendor
 no ipv6 address dhcp
 no ipv6 address autoconfig
! no negotiation auto
!
no ipv6 nd cache expire refresh
no ipv6 unicast-routing


!
! this thing is still enabled by default
no ip forward-protocol nd


! the switch will configure "product-analytics" after being online for 7 days.
! this happens to any switch that is running 17.18.1
! thanks cisco
no product-analyticss


! Linux shell
! Not sure how different this from the Consent Token TAC uses to access a Linux shell
! https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/support/docs/field-notices/641/fn64190.html
install one day platform shell license
conf t
platform shell
end
request platform software system shell rp active


